      "id": "maryland-holidays",
      "sourceUrl": "https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=ggp&section=1-111&enactments=false",
      "title": "The legal holidays of Maryland (Md. Code, Gen. Provis. § 1-111(a)) that\n`us-federal-holidays` does not already close: Lincoln's birthday (February\n12), Maryland Day (March 25), Good Friday, Defenders' Day (September 12),\nAmerican Indian Heritage Day (the Friday after Thanksgiving) and each\nstatewide general election day (the Tuesday after the first Monday in\nNovember of an even year). § 1-111(b) moves only a Sunday holiday, to the\nnext Monday. The section's Martin Luther King, Jr., Memorial and Columbus\nDays are the days Congress designates, and its other days are federal\nholidays. Each `once` day is listed from the date the vendored text was\nretrieved (October 29, 2026) to the end of 2050. Not modeled: a day the\nPresident or the Governor designates for general cessation of business (§\n1-111(a)(18)), which no vendored source lists."
